---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { PERSON } from '../config';
import { path } from '../lib/url';
import { breadcrumbLd } from '../lib/schema';
---

<Layout
  title="How this site is made"
  description="This portfolio is built and maintained with AI and a human in the loop. The work and experience it describes are Atharv Vadehra's own."
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbLd([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'How this site is made' }])]}
>
  <div class="container wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: path('/') }, { name: 'How this site is made' }]} />
    <p class="eyebrow">Transparency</p>
    <h1>How this site is made</h1>
    <p class="lead muted">
      This site is built and maintained with AI, with me in the loop. The projects, experience and ideas on it are
      mine and real. AI helps me do this better and faster; it does not stand in for me.
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The work is authentic.</strong> Every project here is something I built, from my own repositories and my own resume. The AI writes about my work; it does not invent it.</li>
        <li><strong>AI is a tool I use to improve.</strong> I use an AI coding assistant (Claude) to draft write-ups, write and edit the site's code, check that it builds, and tighten wording.</li>
        <li><strong>A human decides.</strong> I choose what to build, supply the source material, review the output, ask for corrections, and approve what gets published.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the AI does</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Reads my project repositories and documentation, and drafts the project pages and blog posts from them.</li>
        <li>Writes and maintains the site's code (the pages, styling, search metadata and feeds).</li>
        <li>Runs the build, checks that links work, and fixes layout problems such as dark-mode contrast.</li>
        <li>Suggests keywords and wording, which I accept, change or reject.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Build the projects themselves: the infrastructure, the honeypots, the detection rules and the rest.</li>
        <li>Decide the story: what each project is for, what I'm trying to learn, and where I want to go next.</li>
        <li>Review and correct. If a draft is hard to read, too technical or not what I mean, I send it back.</li>
        <li>Approve every publish. Nothing goes live without my say-so.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Guardrails against making things up</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Content is written only from facts in my repositories, my resume and what I tell the assistant. Where something is unknown, it should be left out or marked as a plan.</li>
        <li>No invented results. Posts about the honeypots do not quote attack numbers I haven't measured, and the page for my unfinished VLAN design says it has not run on real hardware.</li>
        <li>Claims are checked against my resume. For example, my resume says I collaborated on the RAG pipeline, so the site says that rather than claiming I built it alone.</li>
        <li>Writing that comes from the AI is labelled. Each write-up ends with a note saying so.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why I do it this way</h2>
      <p>
        I'm building towards the point where AI and cybersecurity meet, so it would be odd to avoid AI in my own work. I also
        think the honest way to use it is in the open: it makes me faster and better, and it works best when a person who
        understands the subject is checking it. I want to be someone who can use AI well, not someone replaced by it.
      </p>

      <h2>Spot a mistake?</h2>
      <p>
        Tell me and I'll fix it. You can reach me at <a href={`mailto:${PERSON.email}`}>{PERSON.email}</a> or on
        <a href={PERSON.linkedin} rel="me noopener" target="_blank"> LinkedIn</a>. The site's source is on
        <a href={PERSON.github} rel="me noopener" target="_blank"> GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .wrap { padding-top: 48px; padding-bottom: 32px; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.1rem; max-width: 680px; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .prose { max-width: var(--prose); margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; }
</style>
